.TH KUBERNETES(1) kubernetes User Manuals
Eric Paris
Jan 2015

.SH "نام (NAME)"
kubeadm certs check-expiration \- Check certificates expiration for a Kubernetes cluster


.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBkubeadm certs check-expiration\fP [OPTIONS]


.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Checks expiration for the certificates in the local PKI managed by kubeadm.


.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
\fB--allow-missing-template-keys\fP=true
	If true, ignore any errors in templates when a field or map key is missing in the template. Only applies to golang and jsonpath output formats.

.PP
\fB--cert-dir\fP="/etc/kubernetes/pki"
	The path where to save the certificates

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	Path to a kubeadm configuration file.

.PP
\fB--kubeconfig\fP="/etc/kubernetes/admin.conf"
	The kubeconfig file to use when talking to the cluster. If the flag is not set, a set of standard locations can be searched for an existing kubeconfig file.

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="text"
	Output format. One of: text|json|yaml|kyaml|go-template|go-template-file|template|templatefile|jsonpath|jsonpath-as-json|jsonpath-file.

.PP
\fB--show-managed-fields\fP=false
	If true, keep the managedFields when printing objects in JSON or YAML format.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--rootfs\fP=""
	The path to the 'real' host root filesystem. This will cause kubeadm to chroot into the provided path.

.PP
\fB--version\fP=false
	--version, --version=raw prints version information and quits; --version=vX.Y.Z... sets the reported version


.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBkubeadm-certs(1)\fP,


.SH "تاریخچه (HISTORY)"
